      ],
      "blocks": {
        "faq_question_FCHfrh": {
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>We recommend taking two gummies per serving for the full effect. If you are typically sensitive to digestive supplements, you can start with one gummy and work your way up. Do not exceed a maximum of two servings per day.</p>",
            "title": "How many gummies can I take a day?"
          },
          "type": "faq-question"
        },
        "faq_question_PAxNUn": {
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Bloat Capsules and Bloat Gummies are both designed to support digestion and reduce bloating, just in different formats so you can choose what works best for you. Our original Bloat Capsules come in a traditional capsule form and provide a blend of targeted herbs and enzymes. Bloat Gummies are built around many of the same key herbal ingredients, with the addition of fiber and a clinically studied postbiotic, all in a great tasting gummy. Both are designed to be fast-acting and efficacious so it really comes down to personal preference!</p>",
            "title": "What is the difference between Bloat gummies and Bloat capsules?"
          },
          "type": "faq-question"
        },
        "faq_question_dgiGw9": {
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>If you are pregnant, conceiving, or breastfeeding, we always recommend checking with your doctor before starting a new supplement. </p>",
            "title": "Are Bloat Gummies pregnancy safe?"
          },
          "type": "faq-question"
        },
        "faq_question_gpCYaF": {
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Bloat Gummies are designed to work quickly to help reduce bloating, ease stomach discomfort, and support smoother digestion when you need it most. They can help with that heavy or full feeling after eating, as well as occasional gas and digestive sluggishness. What makes them unique is their combination of fast-acting herbal support, prebiotic fiber, and a clinically-studied postbiotic, so they not only help you feel better in the moment but also support overall gut health over time.</p>",
            "title": "How do Bloat Gummies work?"
          },
          "type": "faq-question"
        },
        "faq_question_kXCcU3": {
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>We recommend storing your Bloat gummies in a tightly sealed container, in a cool, dry place away from sunlight or humidity. Make sure to tightly close your container between uses. </p>",
            "title": "How should I store my Bloat gummies? "
          },
          "type": "faq-question"
        },
        "faq_question_tVeDhD": {
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Bloat Gummies work by combining many of the same core targeted herbs found in our original Bloat Capsules with prebiotic fiber and a clinically-studied postbiotic to support digestion from multiple angles. The herbal blend helps support digestion and reduce bloating quickly, the added scFOS provides a meaningful dose of fiber, and the postbiotic helps support overall gut comfort. Together, this blend helps your body process food more comfortably and reduce bloating and gassiness fast. </p>",
            "title": "What is HT-ES1?"
          },
          "type": "faq-question"
        },
        "faq_question_tXNHwJ": {
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Bloat Gummies can generally be taken with other supplements. If you’re taking multiple digestive products, you may want to space them out to better understand how each one works for you. If you have any specific concerns or have a more complex supplement routine, it’s always a good idea to check with your doctor before starting a new supplement. </p>",
            "title": "Can I take Bloat gummies with other supplements?"
          },
          "type": "faq-question"
        },
        "faq_question_w6RL6w": {
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>No, Bloat Gummies contain 0g of sugar and no sugar alcohols. They’re instead sweetened with a blend of prebiotic fibers like scFOS and acacia fiber, along with Reb M, a zero-calorie sweetener derived from fermented rice. This allows us to create a great-tasting gummy without the need for added sugar or artificial sweeteners.</p>",
            "title": "Do Bloat gummies contain sugar or artificial sweeteners?"
          },
          "type": "faq-question"
        }
      },
      "name": "FAQ",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "Bloat Gummies FAQs",
        "subheading": "What to know before you try"
      },
      "type": "faq"
    },
